[medium] .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml:21 (security)
The workflow changed previously pinned dependencies to mutable refs: setup-opa now uses the moving v2 tag here and in test.yml, and gooci is installed with @latest on line 28. This job has contents/packages write permissions and publishes release/package artifacts, so a moved tag or changed latest module can alter the build or exfiltrate the GitHub token without any repository diff.
Suggested fix: Pin open-policy-agent/setup-opa to a commit SHA in both workflows and install gooci at a fixed audited version, preferably the previous known-good v0.0.7 unless an explicit upgrade is needed.
Guidance: In .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml and .github/workflows/test.yml, replace open-policy-agent/setup-opa@v2 with a full commit SHA for the setup-opa action while keeping the existing with: version: 1.6.0 input. In .github/workflows/build-and-upload.yml, replace `go install github.com/compliance-framework/gooci@latest` with a fixed audited version, preferably `go install github.com/compliance-framework/gooci@v0.0.7` unless the project intentionally needs a newer reviewed release. Do not change the action permissions or artifact publishing behavior as part of this fix; the goal is only to remove mutable executable dependencies from privileged CI jobs.
