[low] Makefile:5 (test quality)
make validate now runs opa check without --strict, while README.md and CI still require opa check --strict policies. Local validation can pass Rego that CI rejects, which weakens the documented developer workflow and makes failures show up later.
Suggested fix: Restore opa check --strict policies in the Makefile, or intentionally update README.md and CI to the same non-strict contract if strict checking is no longer desired.
Guidance: In Makefile, update the validate target from `@opa check policies` to `@opa check --strict policies` so local validation matches README.md and .github/workflows/test.yml. Do not relax README.md or CI; strict checking is already the documented and enforced contract.
